{
  "id": "longest_common_prefix",
  "title": "Longest Common Prefix",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Algorithms",
  "tags": [
    "Array",
    "String",
    "Trie"
  ],
  "description": "<p>Write a function to find the longest common prefix string amongst an array of strings.</p> <p>If there is no common prefix, return an empty string <code>\"\"</code>.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> strs = [\"flower\",\"flow\",\"flight\"]\n<strong>Output:</strong> \"fl\"\n</pre> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> strs = [\"dog\",\"racecar\",\"car\"]\n<strong>Output:</strong> \"\"\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> There is no common prefix among the input strings.\n</pre> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>1 &lt;= strs.length &lt;= 200</code></li> <li><code>0 &lt;= strs[i].length &lt;= 200</code></li> <li><code>strs[i]</code> consists of only lowercase English letters if it is non-empty.</li> </ul>",
  "hints": [],
  "method": {
    "name": "longestCommonPrefix",
    "returnType": "auto",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "strs",
        "type": "array"
      }
    ]
  },
